## Exact Corridor

The G3CX source-observation corridor has 394 components and dimension 2786. Its off-diagonal structure is exactly:

```text
392 singleton rows  -> 1710 core       392 nonzeros
684 core rows       -> 392 singletons  10803 nonzeros
684 core rows       -> 1710 core       17077 nonzeros
```

There are no singleton-to-singleton blocks in this corridor. This makes the characteristic-zero solve a selected three-stage computation rather than a generic 4426-dimensional inversion.

## Theorem

On canonical Archimedean embedding 4, load the G3CZ enclosure for the 1710 core and propagate all 740 G3CX-active source columns through the 392 scalar equations and the 684 core. Then:

- all `392 * 740 = 290080` scalar residual balls contain zero;
- all `684 * 740 = 506160` core-449 residual balls contain zero;
- contraction with the exact path factor `W` emits

```text
Q_active = W A0^(-1) U in C^(988 x 740);
```

- the omitted 248 columns vanish identically over `Q(gamma)` by G3CX;
- the G3CY row and column selections extract

```text
T_Q = Q[R,C] in C^(710 x 710).
```

The directed-rounding determinant ball of `T_Q` excludes zero. This numerical result agrees with the independent exact reason for invertibility: G3CY proved that the same minor is a nonzero element over `Q(gamma)`, and every field embedding is injective.

All coefficients are rational polynomials in `gamma`, so complex conjugation carries the complete result to canonical embedding 5.

## Consequence

On embeddings 4 and 5, the formerly formal second Woodbury data are now actual certified values:

```text
U_Q = Q[:,C]
T_Q = Q[R,C]
W_Q = Q[R,:]
```

The persisted archive stores the 740 nonzero columns. The 248 omitted columns of `W_Q` are exact zeros, not truncations.

This closes characteristic-zero value evaluation of the H11 reduced coupling on one conjugate embedding pair. It does not yet solve the parameter-dependent kernel

```text
